
2
00:00:02,103 --> 00:00:03,304
It's like that, Charlamagne.

3
00:00:04,172 --> 00:00:05,773
You don't think it
kicks in immediately?

4
00:00:05,939 --> 00:00:07,175
No, I don't think
it kicks in like that.

5
00:00:07,341 --> 00:00:08,409
The PEDs don't kick
in immediately?

6
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,000
Official YIFY movies site:
YTS.BZ

7
00:00:08,576 --> 00:00:09,909
No, I don't think
it does like that.

8
00:00:09,910 --> 00:00:11,745
And I don't think
it guarantees that you'll hit
a home run.

9
00:00:11,912 --> 00:00:13,447
Charlamagne would do it
right before the game.

10
00:00:13,614 --> 00:00:14,848
- That's right.
- No.

11
00:00:15,015 --> 00:00:16,584
Now, uh, talk about
the rent in Brooklyn.

12
00:00:16,750 --> 00:00:18,586
Yes, so, the average rent
in Brooklyn now

13
00:00:18,752 --> 00:00:21,789
has soared up to $3,035.

14
00:00:21,955 --> 00:00:23,524
Is that crazy in Brooklyn?

15
00:00:23,691 --> 00:00:25,493
I don't know why anybody
would wanna live--

16
00:00:25,659 --> 00:00:26,760
In the best borough?
I don't know.

17
00:00:26,927 --> 00:00:27,895
For $3,000.

18
00:00:28,062 --> 00:00:29,263
That's $3,000 a month?

19
00:00:29,430 --> 00:00:30,664
- Yes!
- God...

20
00:00:30,831 --> 00:00:32,333
You don't even get grass
in Brooklyn.

21
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:33,834
- Hell no.
- They do so have grass.

22
00:00:34,001 --> 00:00:35,202
You don't have no grass
in Brooklyn.

23
00:00:35,203 --> 00:00:36,970
You know what you can get
in Jersey for $3,000 a month?

24
00:00:37,138 --> 00:00:38,239
That's what I'm trying
to tell him.

25
00:00:38,406 --> 00:00:39,873
You know what you'd be getting
in North Carolina?

26
00:00:40,040 --> 00:00:41,775
- Oh, Lord have mercy.
- Live like a king out there.

27
00:00:41,942 --> 00:00:43,511
We gon' buy
Fantasia's old house.

28
00:00:44,945 --> 00:00:45,713
Wake up, man!

29
00:00:51,219 --> 00:00:52,720
Call an ambulance!

30
00:00:52,886 --> 00:00:53,687
Sir, are you okay?

31
00:00:55,789 --> 00:00:57,325
Hey. Hey, stop!

32
00:00:57,625 --> 00:00:59,093
Oh, my God!

33
00:01:23,016 --> 00:01:24,285
Oh, give me a hint.

34
00:01:24,452 --> 00:01:25,653
My favorite color.

35
00:01:25,819 --> 00:01:27,388
Favorite color's blue.

36
00:01:27,888 --> 00:01:29,223
- What?
- Blue...

37
00:01:29,923 --> 00:01:31,024
Blues singer?

38
00:01:31,192 --> 00:01:33,093
I can't believe you don't know
my favorite color.

39
00:01:33,261 --> 00:01:35,363
- It's blue.
- No, it's green.

40
00:01:35,663 --> 00:01:37,064
Well, it used to be blue.

41
00:01:37,231 --> 00:01:39,066
No. Always green.

42
00:01:39,333 --> 00:01:40,868
Man, what a shame.

43
00:01:41,034 --> 00:01:42,636
Whatever. What's my
favorite color?

44
00:01:42,803 --> 00:01:43,837
- Purple.
- Ehh.

45
00:01:44,104 --> 00:01:45,573
- What?
- Lavender.

46
00:01:46,073 --> 00:01:47,241
Pshht. Same thing.

47
00:01:47,408 --> 00:01:48,942
Definitely not the same thing.

48
00:01:51,945 --> 00:01:54,482
Oh, oh, oh! It's Al Green.

49
00:01:55,849 --> 00:01:56,717
Don't change the subject.

50
00:01:56,884 --> 00:01:57,951
You don't know
my favorite color.

51
00:01:58,118 --> 00:01:59,252
Well, you changed it first.

52
00:01:59,253 --> 00:02:00,854
You still haven't answered
my question about August.

53
00:02:01,422 --> 00:02:03,924
We gotta book a date soon
so we can get a deal.

54
00:02:04,525 --> 00:02:05,759
Yeah, August won't work.

55
00:02:06,059 --> 00:02:07,161
Keith starts school.

56
00:02:07,328 --> 00:02:08,529
We gotta be there
to move him in.

57
00:02:08,696 --> 00:02:09,430
Mhm.

58
00:02:10,498 --> 00:02:12,400
- Mm-hmm.
- What?

59
00:02:13,033 --> 00:02:15,303
From foster care
to four year college.

60
00:02:15,936 --> 00:02:17,037
You did that.

61
00:02:18,472 --> 00:02:19,540
How's it feel?

62
00:02:21,875 --> 00:02:23,277
Can't wrap my head around it.

63
00:02:23,444 --> 00:02:24,445
Hmm.

64
00:02:24,712 --> 00:02:26,314
Gives me the chills
and makes me wanna cry

65
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:27,448
at the same time.

66
00:02:27,615 --> 00:02:28,482
Mm-hmm.

67
00:02:29,049 --> 00:02:30,984
I just gotta make sure
he shows up.

68
00:02:31,785 --> 00:02:32,820
He'll show up.

69
00:02:33,254 --> 00:02:35,989
No, he's been through
too much not to show up.

70
00:02:36,557 --> 00:02:37,791
Yeah, I hope you're right.

71
00:02:39,527 --> 00:02:40,528
I am right.

72
00:02:41,629 --> 00:02:43,531
- Okay? Okay.
- Okay. Okay.

73
00:02:47,868 --> 00:02:48,902
Come on.

74
00:02:49,303 --> 00:02:50,338
Put the cake down.

75
00:02:50,504 --> 00:02:51,505
- What?
- Come here.

76
00:02:51,672 --> 00:02:52,873
- What you doing?
- Come here.

77
00:02:57,845 --> 00:02:58,879
What?

78
00:02:59,046 --> 00:03:00,681
- Dance with me.
- Oh.

79
00:03:00,848 --> 00:03:01,815
Yeah.

80
00:03:01,982 --> 00:03:03,050
- Okay.
- Oh!

81
00:03:03,251 --> 00:03:04,852
Ooh, what was that?

82
00:03:07,321 --> 00:03:10,190
You cannot dance like
that at our wedding.

83
00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:13,861
Oh...

84
00:03:14,862 --> 00:03:18,198
Once your brother moves out,
we get our apartment back.

85
00:03:18,799 --> 00:03:20,301
Mhm. True.

86
00:03:20,468 --> 00:03:22,270
- Our refrigerator.
- Mm-hmm.

87
00:03:22,503 --> 00:03:24,104
The bathroom.

88
00:03:25,473 --> 00:03:27,007
You get your car back.

89
00:03:27,508 --> 00:03:29,410
- Yes, I do.
- Mm-hmm.

90
00:03:35,716 --> 00:03:36,717
What?

91
00:03:38,419 --> 00:03:39,653
What if we moved?

92
00:03:39,820 --> 00:03:41,889
- Moved?
- It's so tight here.

93
00:03:42,356 --> 00:03:43,924
Well, baby, it is New York.

94
00:03:44,091 --> 00:03:45,158
Nobody has space.

95
00:03:45,359 --> 00:03:47,628
Nothing big is remotely
affordable anymore.

96
00:03:47,795 --> 00:03:49,330
Yeah, I can make
some more money.

97
00:03:50,197 --> 00:03:51,965
With Keith gone
and the market up.

98
00:03:52,199 --> 00:03:54,034
My crew's hungry.
A few more projects...

99
00:03:54,201 --> 00:03:55,636
Baby, baby, baby.

100
00:03:56,036 --> 00:03:57,471
Listen to me.

101
00:03:58,005 --> 00:03:59,807
I don't care about more money.

102
00:04:00,341 --> 00:04:02,343
Or the size of our apartment.

103
00:04:04,011 --> 00:04:05,212
I'm getting married.

104
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:07,848
That's all I want.

105
00:04:08,982 --> 00:04:10,451
You and me.

106
00:04:12,920 --> 00:04:14,688
I'm gonna build you
a house one day.

107
00:04:16,657 --> 00:04:17,791
You promise?

108
00:04:23,030 --> 00:04:24,298
From my own hands.

109
00:04:28,001 --> 00:04:29,870
You know how much
I love you, right?

110
00:04:33,173 --> 00:04:34,475
I really do.

111
00:04:38,779 --> 00:04:41,382
♪ Shining so brightly ♪

112
00:04:43,817 --> 00:04:46,520
♪ It's me that's
missing your love ♪

113
00:04:53,827 --> 00:04:54,795
Who is that?

114
00:04:57,598 --> 00:04:58,632
What the...

115
00:04:58,932 --> 00:05:00,634
Who is knocking like that?

116
00:05:27,461 --> 00:05:29,630
Keith? What happened?

117
00:05:29,963 --> 00:05:31,665
What happened?

118
00:05:32,433 --> 00:05:33,934
Bro. What happened?

119
00:05:34,802 --> 00:05:36,269
- I crashed.
- You crashed?

120
00:05:36,437 --> 00:05:37,638
You crashed in my car?

121
00:05:38,338 --> 00:05:40,107
Did somebody else get hurt?

122
00:05:40,441 --> 00:05:41,775
They weren't moving.

123
00:05:41,942 --> 00:05:43,310
No! God.

124
00:05:43,477 --> 00:05:44,878
Keith, are they dead?

125
00:05:45,278 --> 00:05:46,380
They're dead.

126
00:05:46,547 --> 00:05:47,548
Shit!

127
00:05:53,987 --> 00:05:55,055
Keith, let me see.

128
00:05:55,222 --> 00:05:56,457
I can't let this happen.

129
00:05:57,357 --> 00:05:59,393
He'll be okay.
He'll be all right.

130
00:05:59,760 --> 00:06:00,894
What are you doing?

131
00:06:01,061 --> 00:06:02,463
Why are you putting
on his shirt?

132
00:06:03,564 --> 00:06:05,132
- Chris. Stop it.
- Listen.

133
00:06:05,298 --> 00:06:06,299
- Stop it!
- Li-- no.

134
00:06:06,467 --> 00:06:07,768
He got a record, I don't.

135
00:06:07,935 --> 00:06:09,603
- Why are you putting it on?
- I can't let this happen.

136
00:06:09,770 --> 00:06:10,471
No!

137
00:06:10,638 --> 00:06:11,405
Stop it.
Stop it.

138
00:06:11,572 --> 00:06:12,440
Regardless he's going
to jail.

139
00:06:12,606 --> 00:06:14,207
He did it, Chris!
You didn't do it!

140
00:06:14,374 --> 00:06:15,609
You don't know
what we've been through.

141
00:06:15,776 --> 00:06:16,544
What about me?

142
00:06:16,710 --> 00:06:17,978
You gotta trust me, baby.

143
00:06:18,145 --> 00:06:19,279
No, no.

144
00:06:21,114 --> 00:06:22,416
You can't do this.

145
00:06:37,698 --> 00:06:40,133
♪ Shining so bright ♪

146
00:07:05,493 --> 00:07:06,460
Do you have a minute?

147
00:07:07,628 --> 00:07:09,029
I need a big push,
Tara.

148
00:07:10,297 --> 00:07:11,298
Push!

149
00:07:11,465 --> 00:07:13,501
I can see it. Push, Tara.

150
00:07:13,767 --> 00:07:15,268
That's it.

151
00:07:15,435 --> 00:07:16,369
Push!

152
00:07:17,170 --> 00:07:18,872
That's it. That's it.

153
00:07:36,724 --> 00:07:39,092
Christopher Newborn,
the Queens, New York, man

154
00:07:39,259 --> 00:07:41,629
convicted of felony
vehicular manslaughter

155
00:07:41,795 --> 00:07:44,998
after a hit and run in 2011,
is being released today

156
00:07:45,165 --> 00:07:48,168
after the Innocence Project
unearthed video evidence

157
00:07:48,335 --> 00:07:51,338
vindicating Newborn of
an additional murder charge

158
00:07:51,505 --> 00:07:54,041
stemming from a prison
fight in 2013.

159
00:07:54,274 --> 00:07:56,109
Records show Newborn
served nearly

160
00:07:56,276 --> 00:07:58,646
seven consecutive years
in isolation,

161
00:07:58,812 --> 00:08:01,381
placed there unjustly
by guards who framed him

162
00:08:01,549 --> 00:08:03,450
for the murder
of a fellow inmate.

163
00:08:03,617 --> 00:08:06,153
A murder committed
by those very guards.

164
00:08:06,319 --> 00:08:07,855
Now, look, I wanna deal with

165
00:08:08,021 --> 00:08:09,623
the nightmare of him being

166
00:08:09,790 --> 00:08:11,258
thrown
into solitary confinement

167
00:08:11,424 --> 00:08:13,226
after getting framed
by these prison guards.

168
00:08:13,460 --> 00:08:14,928
Seven years in the hole.

169
00:08:15,095 --> 00:08:16,228
Seven.

170
00:08:16,229 --> 00:08:18,365
How does that impact
this brother's mental health?

171
00:08:18,532 --> 00:08:20,000
What does it mean
for his family?

172
00:08:20,167 --> 00:08:22,002
How can he get his life back?

173
00:08:22,202 --> 00:08:24,972
Newborn's case has not only
raised lawsuit flags,

174
00:08:25,138 --> 00:08:27,808
but has launched him into the
center of the ongoing debate

175
00:08:27,975 --> 00:08:30,377
over the inhumane
aspects of isolation

176
00:08:30,544 --> 00:08:32,045
within the prison system.

177
00:09:14,822 --> 00:09:16,089
Just over here.
One question!

178
00:09:16,256 --> 00:09:17,825
- Come on.
- Chris, over here!

179
00:09:21,261 --> 00:09:22,763
Chris,
do you feel justice?

180
00:09:22,930 --> 00:09:25,599
Will there be a lawsuit
against the State of New York?

181
00:10:21,722 --> 00:10:23,023
Hey, Jake, get up here.

182
00:10:23,523 --> 00:10:24,524
Ready?

183
00:10:25,425 --> 00:10:26,526
Lean in, everyone.

184
00:10:26,694 --> 00:10:28,628
On one, two, three,
say cheese.

185
00:10:30,263 --> 00:10:31,198
Aww.

186
00:10:35,736 --> 00:10:37,304
You swipe your finger.

187
00:10:40,107 --> 00:10:41,208
Like that.

188
00:10:44,544 --> 00:10:45,578
All right, buckle up, Jake.

189
00:11:48,408 --> 00:11:49,609
Still nothing.

190
00:11:49,777 --> 00:11:50,911
He's been better.

191
00:11:51,845 --> 00:11:54,047
I mean, especially lately.
More responsive.

192
00:11:55,115 --> 00:11:57,684
They say he can come out
of it. That-that he...

193
00:11:58,318 --> 00:11:59,753
that he can talk.

194
00:12:00,520 --> 00:12:01,755
But...

195
00:12:02,756 --> 00:12:05,558
now the longer he doesn't,
the more chance he never will.

196
00:12:07,727 --> 00:12:09,329
What's that thing he squeezes?

197
00:12:09,763 --> 00:12:10,798
It's clay.

198
00:12:11,031 --> 00:12:12,900
It's part of clay art therapy.

199
00:12:13,066 --> 00:12:15,668
A doctor suggested it
a few years ago, and it stuck.

200
00:12:16,136 --> 00:12:17,637
And he just squeezes it?

201
00:12:17,805 --> 00:12:18,972
Sometimes, yeah.

202
00:12:19,139 --> 00:12:20,740
When he's coping
or calming down.

203
00:12:21,008 --> 00:12:22,642
He makes stuff too. See?

204
00:12:24,511 --> 00:12:26,013
My God. He did that?

205
00:12:26,179 --> 00:12:27,114
Yeah.

206
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:28,681
The way you're good at
building things,

207
00:12:28,849 --> 00:12:30,150
that's how he is with clay.

208
00:12:31,118 --> 00:12:32,285
Has it helped?

209
00:12:32,452 --> 00:12:34,254
With the, uh, the seizures?

210
00:12:34,421 --> 00:12:35,488
I think so.

211
00:12:36,423 --> 00:12:38,325
That and the-the medicine.

212
00:12:39,092 --> 00:12:40,994
No seizures so far this year.

213
00:12:48,836 --> 00:12:50,370
Come back here!

214
00:13:12,993 --> 00:13:14,862
You grew up on me.

215
00:13:17,330 --> 00:13:19,332
Last time I saw you,
you were--

216
00:13:42,789 --> 00:13:44,757
You used to love
to dance with me.

217
00:13:45,525 --> 00:13:47,227
You were never
very good, but...

218
00:13:47,861 --> 00:13:49,129
at least you tried.

219
00:13:50,163 --> 00:13:51,731
If I was bad back then...

220
00:13:52,799 --> 00:13:54,667
- Imagine now.
- I'm kidding.

221
00:13:56,870 --> 00:13:58,705
I love the way you move.

222
00:14:01,208 --> 00:14:02,509
I almost forgot.

223
00:14:08,081 --> 00:14:09,082
Open it.

224
00:14:12,785 --> 00:14:14,287
It's the first time
the three of us

225
00:14:14,454 --> 00:14:15,522
have been in
a picture together.

226
00:14:16,056 --> 00:14:17,490
Uh, Chris Newborn.

227
00:14:17,657 --> 00:14:19,026
So sorry to interrupt.

228
00:14:19,192 --> 00:14:20,193
Matt Walton.

229
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:22,195
Look, I heard about
what happened to you,

230
00:14:22,362 --> 00:14:23,596
and I think it's just...

231
00:14:23,863 --> 00:14:25,999
awful, and I think the state
should be held accountable.

232
00:14:26,499 --> 00:14:28,835
Now, my firm, Bregmen,
Foss and Associates,

233
00:14:29,002 --> 00:14:30,270
is both effective
and affordable--

234
00:14:30,437 --> 00:14:31,604
Not interested.

235
00:14:36,176 --> 00:14:37,244
Fair enough.

236
00:14:39,546 --> 00:14:40,713
Well, uh...

237
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:42,749
I see you're enjoying dinner,
so I will just leave you

238
00:14:42,916 --> 00:14:44,217
my card, and if you do
change your mind--

239
00:14:44,384 --> 00:14:45,552
Not interested.

240
00:14:47,054 --> 00:14:47,955
Chris!

241
00:14:48,121 --> 00:14:49,422
We are not in danger, baby.

242
00:14:49,756 --> 00:14:52,192
Think about our family,
think about Jake.

243
00:14:55,762 --> 00:14:56,896
That's right.

244
00:14:57,830 --> 00:14:58,999
Now breathe, baby.

245
00:15:00,433 --> 00:15:01,668
Breathe.

246
00:15:29,329 --> 00:15:30,863
You gonna let me in?
Or...

247
00:15:35,635 --> 00:15:37,104
Chris, what we doin'?

248
00:15:39,139 --> 00:15:40,373
I know you hear me.

249
00:15:49,016 --> 00:15:50,117
Welcome home.

250
00:16:07,834 --> 00:16:09,169
My old digs.

251
00:16:11,604 --> 00:16:13,140
Memories in this place.

252
00:16:19,179 --> 00:16:20,413
How'd you know I got out?

253
00:16:20,580 --> 00:16:22,515
It's all they're
talking about on the news.

254
00:16:22,949 --> 00:16:24,951
Video of how they
framed you is everywhere.

255
00:16:26,119 --> 00:16:27,754
We always knew
you were innocent.

256
00:16:28,388 --> 00:16:29,589
Didn't make no sense.

257
00:16:30,623 --> 00:16:32,259
No one just snaps
and murders someone

258
00:16:32,425 --> 00:16:33,626
just before release.

259
00:16:34,694 --> 00:16:36,729
Saying you got a real
chance at a lawsuit.

260
00:16:37,597 --> 00:16:39,066
How it could be
in the millions.

261
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:42,835
Saying how shocked they are
you survived the hole.

262
00:16:44,003 --> 00:16:45,372
I wasn't surprised though.

263
00:16:46,106 --> 00:16:47,140
Then again,

264
00:16:48,508 --> 00:16:49,642
I know you.

265
00:16:52,112 --> 00:16:53,646
Nothing can break my big bro.

266
00:16:55,115 --> 00:16:56,083
Jake.

267
00:16:56,649 --> 00:16:58,251
Come say hi
to your uncle Keith.

268
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:01,721
How you doing, little man?

269
00:17:05,692 --> 00:17:07,760
Tara will be home
from work soon, so...

270
00:17:08,095 --> 00:17:10,097
And you don't want me around
when she gets here?

271
00:17:13,333 --> 00:17:15,068
I ain't ask you
to go away from me.

272
00:17:15,268 --> 00:17:17,070
- You didn't have to.
- Oh, right.

273
00:17:17,237 --> 00:17:18,238
'Cause that's what you do, huh?

274
00:17:18,405 --> 00:17:20,307
- Keith.
- The heroic big bro.

275
00:17:20,473 --> 00:17:22,008
Flies in to save his
two-time loser brother.

276
00:17:22,175 --> 00:17:23,041
Can't do this right now.

277
00:17:23,042 --> 00:17:24,144
I guess I should be
saying thanks.

278
00:17:24,311 --> 00:17:25,278
Stop!

279
00:17:32,685 --> 00:17:34,287
Stop.

280
00:17:36,756 --> 00:17:38,591
Not exactly how
I thought this would go.

281
00:17:40,727 --> 00:17:42,162
I guess it is what it is.

282
00:17:46,233 --> 00:17:47,667
That's my cue, huh?

283
00:17:51,338 --> 00:17:52,539
All right, little man.

284
00:18:17,864 --> 00:18:19,199
Jake.

285
00:18:20,167 --> 00:18:21,568
- Hey, boys.
- Tara!

286
00:18:23,136 --> 00:18:24,671
T-Tara. I--

287
00:18:25,572 --> 00:18:27,607
Let's get you on your side.
All right.

288
00:18:27,774 --> 00:18:29,642
One, two, three.
All right, I got you.

289
00:18:29,976 --> 00:18:31,978
- Is he okay?
- He's all right.

290
00:18:34,447 --> 00:18:35,515
There you go.

291
00:18:36,048 --> 00:18:37,116
Look at me, baby.

292
00:18:37,917 --> 00:18:38,951
Hey.

293
00:18:41,421 --> 00:18:42,689
Are you okay?

294
00:18:43,089 --> 00:18:44,191
Just breathe.

295
00:18:45,258 --> 00:18:46,359
All right?

296
00:18:55,535 --> 00:18:56,736
How is he?

297
00:19:01,308 --> 00:19:02,409
He's fine.

298
00:19:04,311 --> 00:19:05,412
Just...

299
00:19:06,179 --> 00:19:07,747
mostly scared.

300
00:19:10,983 --> 00:19:12,485
I'm gonna ask you something.

301
00:19:14,187 --> 00:19:15,288
And...

302
00:19:17,490 --> 00:19:20,527
if you're not into it,
just say so.

303
00:19:21,561 --> 00:19:22,762
I'll be fine with it.

304
00:19:24,364 --> 00:19:25,965
How would you feel
about a trip?

305
00:19:30,303 --> 00:19:32,472
- A trip?
- Yeah. Like, uh...

306
00:19:33,973 --> 00:19:36,108
Like a break from the city.

307
00:19:36,276 --> 00:19:39,111
Someplace that has space
and fresh air.

308
00:19:39,346 --> 00:19:40,347
I--

309
00:19:40,847 --> 00:19:41,947
I don't feel comfortable,

310
00:19:41,948 --> 00:19:44,251
you paying for something
like that without my help.

311
00:19:45,485 --> 00:19:46,719
Ella's husband.

312
00:19:47,119 --> 00:19:48,621
He works real estate.

313
00:19:49,155 --> 00:19:52,259
The company he's with,
they own a resort up north.

314
00:19:54,126 --> 00:19:55,295
It's a quiet town.

315
00:19:55,762 --> 00:19:57,530
It's already closed
for renovations.

316
00:19:58,465 --> 00:20:00,700
She offered. Two weeks.

317
00:20:02,101 --> 00:20:03,670
There'll be no one
there but us.

318
00:20:05,505 --> 00:20:07,274
I think it could be
good for you.

319
00:20:09,108 --> 00:20:10,910
I think it could be
good for Jake.

320
00:20:14,381 --> 00:20:15,482
For us.

321
00:20:19,819 --> 00:20:20,920
A trip.

322
00:20:22,989 --> 00:20:24,056
A trip.

323
00:21:23,215 --> 00:21:24,517
I'll assume you're Tara.

324
00:21:24,684 --> 00:21:26,052
- Tara. Yes.
- Tara.

325
00:21:26,218 --> 00:21:28,321
Ken Hershey.
Friends call me Hersh.

326
00:21:29,055 --> 00:21:30,056
Chris?

327
00:21:31,090 --> 00:21:32,525
You must be Big Jake.

328
00:21:32,992 --> 00:21:34,293
He's not much of a talker.

329
00:21:34,694 --> 00:21:36,929
You know that some of the best
men this country's ever known

330
00:21:37,096 --> 00:21:38,565
were men of very few words.

331
00:21:38,765 --> 00:21:40,299
Maybe while you're here,
you could be my extra

332
00:21:40,467 --> 00:21:41,868
set of eyes, sorta...

333
00:21:42,168 --> 00:21:44,704
like a junior
security officer.

334
00:21:44,871 --> 00:21:46,473
Hmm. Oh...

335
00:21:46,639 --> 00:21:47,674
Take it.

336
00:21:50,710 --> 00:21:52,044
You got a special one there.

337
00:21:52,845 --> 00:21:54,681
You wanna have a look around?
Come on.

338
00:21:57,149 --> 00:22:00,787
We got two wings,
connected in the lobby here.

339
00:22:02,154 --> 00:22:05,224
The east wing is
the functional hotel
where you'll be.

340
00:22:05,792 --> 00:22:08,695
And, uh, west Wing, you can
see is down due to a reno.

341
00:22:08,861 --> 00:22:10,497
Nothing very exciting
to see there.

342
00:22:10,930 --> 00:22:12,231
Let's show you to your rooms.

343
00:22:22,308 --> 00:22:23,376
Oh.

344
00:22:24,444 --> 00:22:26,112
Oh, my God.

345
00:22:26,746 --> 00:22:28,080
It is gorgeous.

346
00:22:28,247 --> 00:22:30,049
Yeah. Imperial suite.

347
00:22:30,683 --> 00:22:32,284
I mean, uh, it's huge.

348
00:22:32,585 --> 00:22:33,386
Yeah.

349
00:22:33,753 --> 00:22:35,455
You mind if I steal Chris?

350
00:22:35,622 --> 00:22:36,856
Show him the rest
of the property.

351
00:22:37,056 --> 00:22:39,459
Uh, of course.
Yeah. I'll-I'll get, um...

352
00:22:39,626 --> 00:22:40,793
I'll get Jake settled in.

353
00:22:41,260 --> 00:22:42,595
I'll show you how
everything works.

354
00:22:43,195 --> 00:22:44,296
See you in a minute.

355
00:22:45,965 --> 00:22:48,134
Anything you can't handle
at all, just let me know.

356
00:22:48,300 --> 00:22:50,269
I'm just a mile south
down the main road.

357
00:22:52,171 --> 00:22:53,973
Being out of season,
not many people around.

358
00:22:54,206 --> 00:22:55,442
Wild animals?

359
00:22:55,675 --> 00:22:59,311
Oh, sure. We got raccoons,
and the odd wolf. Black bear.

360
00:23:00,179 --> 00:23:01,247
You probably won't see them.

361
00:23:01,414 --> 00:23:03,182
They mostly mind
their own business.

362
00:23:04,451 --> 00:23:06,018
So nothing too dangerous, right?

363
00:23:06,753 --> 00:23:08,521
Nothing more dangerous
than you or me.

364
00:23:16,629 --> 00:23:18,364
I guess you've been
wondering where I've been

365
00:23:18,531 --> 00:23:19,532
these past years.

366
00:23:21,333 --> 00:23:23,102
Why I wasn't here
with you and your mom.

367
00:23:28,908 --> 00:23:30,209
I made a decision.

368
00:23:32,612 --> 00:23:34,046
A decision I might've...

369
00:23:34,647 --> 00:23:37,349
considered differently had
I known you were on the way.

370
00:23:41,387 --> 00:23:42,589
I guess,

371
00:23:43,222 --> 00:23:44,991
I can't change the past,
but...

372
00:23:46,993 --> 00:23:50,463
What I can do is promise you
I will never leave you again.

373
00:23:52,198 --> 00:23:54,534
I will never let anything
happen to you.

374
00:23:56,603 --> 00:23:58,004
I love you, son.

375
00:24:00,239 --> 00:24:02,775
And your mother.
More than anything.

376
00:24:04,310 --> 00:24:06,913
And I'm gonna keep doing
the best I can to prove it.

377
00:24:17,990 --> 00:24:19,726
All right, uh...

378
00:24:22,194 --> 00:24:25,131
Let's get through this, uh,
once and if you don't like it,

379
00:24:25,297 --> 00:24:26,899
or if I'm no good at it,

380
00:24:27,166 --> 00:24:30,269
just pretend to fall asleep
or something. All right?

381
00:24:36,208 --> 00:24:38,811
Oh. You a comedian now.

382
00:25:22,889 --> 00:25:24,190
Do you like it here?

383
00:25:25,925 --> 00:25:26,926
Yeah.

384
00:25:27,827 --> 00:25:29,228
More than I thought I would.

385
00:25:31,030 --> 00:25:32,331
Yeah, me too.

386
00:25:34,400 --> 00:25:35,968
Reminds me

387
00:25:36,669 --> 00:25:39,505
that there's a whole world
outside of the city.

388
00:25:39,739 --> 00:25:41,273
Never thought I'd see the day
when the die-hard

389
00:25:41,440 --> 00:25:42,541
Queens native

390
00:25:42,709 --> 00:25:44,443
would entertain the idea
of leaving.

391
00:25:46,112 --> 00:25:48,848
All right, I'm always
gonna be from Queens, okay?

392
00:25:49,882 --> 00:25:50,917
- Okay?
- Okay.

393
00:25:51,083 --> 00:25:52,118
- Okay.
- Okay.

394
00:25:58,390 --> 00:26:01,260
Oh, my goodness, Jake,
this looks amazing.

395
00:26:01,527 --> 00:26:03,095
Did you do this
all by yourself?

396
00:26:48,574 --> 00:26:49,709
Look at you.

397
00:27:33,853 --> 00:27:35,187
What's wrong, baby?

398
00:27:36,022 --> 00:27:37,089
I don't know.

399
00:27:39,558 --> 00:27:40,559
Um...

400
00:27:41,828 --> 00:27:44,630
Oh... it's okay,
it's okay, it's okay.

401
00:27:44,797 --> 00:27:45,798
You're okay.

402
00:27:46,032 --> 00:27:47,499
It's okay. Okay?

403
00:27:47,666 --> 00:27:48,901
- Yeah.
- Look at me.

404
00:27:49,501 --> 00:27:51,437
- Yeah.
- You're with me, it's okay.

405
00:27:53,239 --> 00:27:54,306
Okay.

406
00:28:06,585 --> 00:28:07,653
Okay, baby.

407
00:28:08,320 --> 00:28:09,588
- Okay.
- I'm sorry.

408
00:28:09,756 --> 00:28:11,090
It's okay.
Don't be sorry.

409
00:28:11,323 --> 00:28:12,258
- I'm sorry.
- No.

410
00:28:12,424 --> 00:28:13,826
No, no, no, no,
don't be sorry.

411
00:28:13,993 --> 00:28:15,427
This is not your fault.

412
00:28:18,264 --> 00:28:19,331
We can...

413
00:28:21,533 --> 00:28:23,102
We can, we can wait.

414
00:28:24,070 --> 00:28:25,437
Until you're ready.

415
00:28:26,505 --> 00:28:28,741
It's just...
been a long time.

416
00:28:30,877 --> 00:28:31,978
I know.

417
00:28:41,453 --> 00:28:42,688
Have you, uh...

418
00:28:44,190 --> 00:28:46,292
thought-thought
at all about the...

419
00:28:47,726 --> 00:28:49,428
the lawsuit?

420
00:28:51,898 --> 00:28:54,633
- Lawsuit?
- Yeah, against, um, the state.

421
00:28:54,901 --> 00:28:56,302
The Bureau of Prisons.

422
00:28:57,336 --> 00:29:00,439
What-what they did
to you, baby,
what they did to you was,

423
00:29:00,606 --> 00:29:02,608
it's not right to our family.

424
00:29:02,775 --> 00:29:03,843
It is not right.

425
00:29:04,010 --> 00:29:05,244
Someone needs
to be held accountable.

426
00:29:05,411 --> 00:29:06,913
And if it's, if it's true,
what they're saying,

427
00:29:07,079 --> 00:29:08,747
that there could be
a settlement, that could--

428
00:29:09,581 --> 00:29:11,583
that could mean a new life.

429
00:29:13,052 --> 00:29:15,487
It could mean
more support for Jake.

430
00:29:16,255 --> 00:29:19,158
Give him the best chance
at the best treatment.

431
00:29:19,758 --> 00:29:20,860
Could--

432
00:29:21,593 --> 00:29:24,663
Could get us all
the help we need.

433
00:29:24,964 --> 00:29:26,732
I-I wouldn't, I wouldn't
know where to begin.

434
00:29:26,899 --> 00:29:28,534
Okay, baby, that's okay.

435
00:29:31,003 --> 00:29:32,504
I can do some research.

436
00:29:32,839 --> 00:29:35,707
You know, I could, I could
see what our options are.

437
00:29:41,914 --> 00:29:42,949
Okay.

438
00:29:44,483 --> 00:29:47,053
- Okay?
- Yeah. Okay.

439
00:30:01,500 --> 00:30:02,568
Hello?

440
00:32:06,959 --> 00:32:08,094
Yeah.

441
00:32:08,260 --> 00:32:08,995
Hey.

442
00:32:09,761 --> 00:32:10,729
Hey.

443
00:32:11,263 --> 00:32:12,431
Yeah, I brought you
some goodies.

444
00:32:12,598 --> 00:32:13,665
Some veggies from the garden.

445
00:32:13,832 --> 00:32:14,766
Where's Jake?

446
00:32:15,767 --> 00:32:17,103
Uh, inside.

447
00:32:19,571 --> 00:32:21,407
You, uh, settling in okay?

448
00:32:21,974 --> 00:32:23,475
Yeah. Just fine.

449
00:32:24,376 --> 00:32:26,645
Well, you chose a beautiful
day for a jog.

450
00:32:30,049 --> 00:32:31,750
All right, I'm gonna head out.

451
00:32:31,917 --> 00:32:34,020
Finish binge-watching Ozark.

452
00:32:34,953 --> 00:32:35,988
If you need me, I'm just--

453
00:32:36,155 --> 00:32:38,057
A mile south on the main road.
Yeah, we know.

454
00:32:38,390 --> 00:32:39,891
All right.

455
00:32:42,361 --> 00:32:44,330
- Thanks.
- You bet.

456
00:32:55,141 --> 00:32:56,308
That was rude.

457
00:32:58,110 --> 00:32:59,645
There's something about him.

458
00:32:59,945 --> 00:33:01,147
I don't know.

459
00:33:03,415 --> 00:33:04,983
Let me know when
he comes around, okay?

460
00:33:06,052 --> 00:33:07,586
Yeah. Okay.

461
00:34:20,126 --> 00:34:22,794
I got a letter from your mom
when you turned five.

462
00:34:24,396 --> 00:34:26,465
They'd been blocking
my mail for years.

463
00:34:27,799 --> 00:34:29,135
But this one got through.

464
00:34:30,636 --> 00:34:32,471
She said you still
hadn't spoke yet.

465
00:34:33,572 --> 00:34:35,174
And I knew that was on me.

466
00:34:36,708 --> 00:34:38,477
The world being what it is,

467
00:34:39,878 --> 00:34:41,580
if I had just
been there for you,

468
00:34:42,681 --> 00:34:45,151
maybe things would've
been different.

469
00:34:48,820 --> 00:34:51,157
You're my mission.
You know that?

470
00:34:52,591 --> 00:34:54,926
From now on, we face
the world together, aight?

471
00:34:59,998 --> 00:35:01,633
Did you just give me
a direct answer?

472
00:35:27,926 --> 00:35:31,730
Two years in, days from
release, you intervene
as guards

473
00:35:31,897 --> 00:35:33,899
beat a man to death.

474
00:35:34,666 --> 00:35:37,936
This is video that has been
widely circulated

475
00:35:38,103 --> 00:35:40,105
which proves you acted
in self-defense.

476
00:35:41,973 --> 00:35:43,809
If those men didn't
frame you, Chris,

477
00:35:43,975 --> 00:35:46,111
you would've been headed home
to be with your family.

478
00:35:46,278 --> 00:35:48,046
Instead, you get
a life sentence.

479
00:35:48,480 --> 00:35:50,081
Worse, to hide their crimes,

480
00:35:50,249 --> 00:35:52,884
they bury you in solitary
confinement to be forgotten.

481
00:35:53,885 --> 00:35:56,021
No visitation, no programs.

482
00:35:56,188 --> 00:35:58,390
Seven years of hell.

483
00:35:59,658 --> 00:36:00,959
Those are the details.

484
00:36:01,126 --> 00:36:04,230
Details that will give
the court just a small idea

485
00:36:04,630 --> 00:36:06,465
of the tragedy
that you've endured.

486
00:36:26,652 --> 00:36:28,754
I'm ready to kill
somebody today!

487
00:36:28,920 --> 00:36:30,121
You think you can touch me?

488
00:36:30,289 --> 00:36:32,958
Come get me!
You cannot come in here!

489
00:36:33,124 --> 00:36:34,293
Come get me! Come!

490
00:37:59,244 --> 00:38:00,912
What the hell
are you doing here?

491
00:38:02,381 --> 00:38:03,582
Great to see you, too.

492
00:38:03,749 --> 00:38:04,683
Who brought you here?

493
00:38:05,083 --> 00:38:06,452
You need to call him back.

494
00:38:09,721 --> 00:38:11,523
What is this, déjà vu?

495
00:38:14,693 --> 00:38:15,794
Of course you're high.

496
00:38:16,695 --> 00:38:18,129
Come on, get inside.

497
00:38:37,182 --> 00:38:38,283
No suite?

498
00:38:39,918 --> 00:38:41,453
Whoever brought you here,
you need to call him

499
00:38:41,620 --> 00:38:42,754
to come get you.

500
00:38:44,856 --> 00:38:46,692
You at all curious
how this happened?

501
00:38:47,058 --> 00:38:48,960
Something to do with
the needle marks on your arm?

502
00:38:50,662 --> 00:38:52,097
Someone came looking for you.

503
00:38:53,465 --> 00:38:54,633
Day after I saw you.

504
00:38:55,200 --> 00:38:57,202
- Looking for me?
- Two guys.

505
00:38:58,069 --> 00:38:59,505
They knew I was your brother.

506
00:38:59,671 --> 00:39:01,573
Looked like they could've
been law enforcement.

507
00:39:01,973 --> 00:39:03,542
Asked questions about you.

508
00:39:04,209 --> 00:39:05,210
Me.

509
00:39:05,811 --> 00:39:07,446
- Our family.
- What'd you tell 'em?

510
00:39:12,551 --> 00:39:14,453
It would've been worse,
but I ran.

511
00:39:19,691 --> 00:39:20,826
How'd you know I was here?

512
00:39:20,992 --> 00:39:22,894
Tara told the neighbor
across the hall.

513
00:39:23,662 --> 00:39:25,130
In case of emergency.

514
00:39:26,898 --> 00:39:27,999
These guys...

515
00:39:28,534 --> 00:39:30,335
I think they had something
to do with your case.

516
00:39:38,477 --> 00:39:39,511
Hey, son.

517
00:39:40,712 --> 00:39:42,380
What you doing here,
you can't sleep?

518
00:39:46,184 --> 00:39:48,654
Uncle Keith may stay here
for a few days.

519
00:39:48,954 --> 00:39:50,789
Uh... he's sick,

520
00:39:51,122 --> 00:39:52,891
and we're gonna
look after him, aight?

521
00:39:53,625 --> 00:39:54,993
What up, nephew?

522
00:39:56,595 --> 00:39:58,464
Probably best we don't tell
your mom about this.

523
00:39:58,630 --> 00:40:00,632
I got a feeling he's not
the snitching type.

524
00:40:00,799 --> 00:40:02,901
She might not think he's
the best influence on you.

525
00:40:06,404 --> 00:40:07,673
Come on, let's head back.

526
00:40:10,375 --> 00:40:11,376
Chris.

527
00:40:13,211 --> 00:40:14,546
No matter what happens,

528
00:40:15,681 --> 00:40:17,048
just keep Jake safe.

529
00:40:18,584 --> 00:40:19,618
Safe from who?

530
00:40:21,319 --> 00:40:22,387
Everyone.

531
00:40:25,691 --> 00:40:28,093
Your Uncle Keith,
he was the type of kid

532
00:40:28,259 --> 00:40:30,361
that after he watched
a superhero movie,

533
00:40:30,596 --> 00:40:32,531
he became that character.

534
00:40:32,698 --> 00:40:34,132
Superpowers and all.

535
00:40:35,166 --> 00:40:38,504
This one time,
he's like... six.

536
00:40:38,770 --> 00:40:41,206
We're home alone
watching Spider-Man.

537
00:40:41,640 --> 00:40:43,642
And within five minutes,
he's climbing the walls.

538
00:40:43,809 --> 00:40:46,411
So, I'm thinking...
he's occupied.

539
00:40:46,878 --> 00:40:48,313
So, I started doing
my homework.

540
00:40:48,480 --> 00:40:49,548
Little did I know,

541
00:40:49,715 --> 00:40:52,217
that this genius has
unplugged the cable cord,

542
00:40:52,383 --> 00:40:54,352
and tied it to this huge
"if you touch it,

543
00:40:54,520 --> 00:40:56,021
we will kill you"
china cabinet.

544
00:40:56,187 --> 00:40:57,656
Nuh-uh.

545
00:40:58,089 --> 00:40:59,791
So, I'm studying or whatever,

546
00:40:59,958 --> 00:41:02,193
and I hear what sounds like
a truck crashing

547
00:41:02,360 --> 00:41:03,461
in the front room.

548
00:41:03,795 --> 00:41:06,397
So, I run in there,
and here's Keith.

549
00:41:06,898 --> 00:41:08,567
Spider-Man underwear on,

550
00:41:08,867 --> 00:41:11,169
stocking over his head,
standing over this

551
00:41:11,336 --> 00:41:14,405
collapsed china cabinet
and broken glass everywhere.

552
00:41:14,573 --> 00:41:15,774
Oh, no.

553
00:41:16,007 --> 00:41:16,808
- It gets worse.
- Nuh-uh.

554
00:41:16,975 --> 00:41:17,743
It gets worse.

555
00:41:17,909 --> 00:41:19,344
At exactly that moment,

556
00:41:19,911 --> 00:41:22,313
our foster parents' car
pulls up in the driveway.

557
00:41:22,480 --> 00:41:23,815
Oh, God.
What did you do?

558
00:41:24,182 --> 00:41:25,851
Would any sensible
11 year old would do.

559
00:41:26,017 --> 00:41:27,252
I knocked some pictures
off the wall,

560
00:41:27,418 --> 00:41:28,554
told 'em it was
an earthquake.

561
00:41:28,720 --> 00:41:29,855
In Brooklyn.

562
00:41:30,021 --> 00:41:31,156
Made sense in my head.

563
00:41:32,824 --> 00:41:34,025
But, yeah.

564
00:41:34,492 --> 00:41:36,762
We didn't last much longer
with that family.

565
00:41:46,872 --> 00:41:47,739
You good?

566
00:41:48,206 --> 00:41:49,340
Yeah.

567
00:41:50,308 --> 00:41:51,810
I'm gonna use the ladies room.

568
00:41:53,144 --> 00:41:55,080
Don't get any ideas
from your father.

569
00:42:30,548 --> 00:42:32,050
Hey, Jake. Come on.

570
00:42:39,858 --> 00:42:40,926
Hey!

571
00:43:50,395 --> 00:43:51,830
I got a call.

572
00:43:53,398 --> 00:43:54,499
From Ella.

573
00:43:56,868 --> 00:43:58,203
She needed to talk.

574
00:43:58,870 --> 00:44:00,571
I shouldn't have left you,
I just--

575
00:44:01,840 --> 00:44:02,941
I'm sorry.

576
00:44:04,943 --> 00:44:06,011
Hersh.

577
00:44:07,278 --> 00:44:08,680
How'd he know we were here?

578
00:44:09,848 --> 00:44:10,849
I called him.

579
00:44:12,583 --> 00:44:13,551
You have his number?

580
00:44:14,152 --> 00:44:16,087
He gave it to us both, Cris.

581
00:44:18,323 --> 00:44:20,091
They would've arrested you.
I--

582
00:44:21,026 --> 00:44:23,695
I figured he could help.

583
00:45:01,900 --> 00:45:03,201
Change of clothes.

584
00:45:15,914 --> 00:45:17,715
What you mean by
what you said last night?

585
00:45:19,584 --> 00:45:21,186
About keeping Jake safe?

586
00:45:24,522 --> 00:45:26,324
The guys who came
looking for you.

587
00:45:29,928 --> 00:45:31,429
They asked about you.

588
00:45:33,932 --> 00:45:34,933
And Jake.

589
00:45:39,570 --> 00:45:41,206
But they never asked
where you were.

590
00:45:46,377 --> 00:45:48,279
They just told me
to stay away from you.

591
00:45:52,183 --> 00:45:53,885
That they wanted you
to be alone.

592
00:45:56,955 --> 00:45:58,089
Isolated.

593
00:46:00,358 --> 00:46:01,993
Vulnerable.

594
00:46:04,462 --> 00:46:06,431
That's why I knew
I had to come find you.

595
00:46:10,802 --> 00:46:12,770
So whatever they were
coming at you with,

596
00:46:14,072 --> 00:46:15,673
you wouldn't have to
face 'em alone.

597
00:46:24,549 --> 00:46:26,317
I had a dream I OD'd.

598
00:46:29,587 --> 00:46:31,222
I'm tired of this ride, bro.

599
00:46:35,593 --> 00:46:36,828
I'm ready to get off.

600
00:47:17,402 --> 00:47:18,436
Hey.

601
00:47:19,470 --> 00:47:20,471
Hey.

602
00:47:20,705 --> 00:47:22,273
- Mmm.
- Where are you?

603
00:47:36,321 --> 00:47:37,455
What did I do?

604
00:47:48,033 --> 00:47:50,768
I feel, I feel so alone here.

605
00:47:54,405 --> 00:47:57,976
Let the two of us on,
on two separate trips.

606
00:48:00,445 --> 00:48:02,247
I know. Hey, I know, I know.

607
00:48:03,414 --> 00:48:04,649
I know there's
a lot that you're

608
00:48:04,815 --> 00:48:05,984
still trying to figure out.

609
00:48:06,151 --> 00:48:07,986
And I don't wanna
get in the way of that.

610
00:48:09,820 --> 00:48:11,089
What do you want?

611
00:48:15,626 --> 00:48:16,794
Your love.

612
00:48:19,030 --> 00:48:20,031
That's all.

613
00:48:23,134 --> 00:48:24,502
Do you love me still?

614
00:48:27,738 --> 00:48:28,739
Yeah.

615
00:48:29,874 --> 00:48:30,976
I love you.

616
00:48:40,018 --> 00:48:41,086
Yeah, okay.

617
00:48:44,089 --> 00:48:45,090
Okay.

618
00:48:46,857 --> 00:48:47,892
Okay.

619
00:50:03,968 --> 00:50:05,503
If you've seen it
in your mind,

620
00:50:05,970 --> 00:50:08,139
you can create it
and you can get there

621
00:50:09,707 --> 00:50:11,242
from right here.

622
00:50:13,711 --> 00:50:15,113
Protect your mind, son.

623
00:50:15,946 --> 00:50:17,282
It's your greatest asset.

624
00:50:18,883 --> 00:50:20,051
Hey.

625
00:50:21,819 --> 00:50:24,922
You don't let nobody walk
through it with dirty feet.

626
00:50:25,956 --> 00:50:27,024
You hear me?

627
00:50:28,393 --> 00:50:31,262
Protect your mind.

628
00:51:01,792 --> 00:51:02,827
We're here.

629
00:51:03,861 --> 00:51:04,895
Stay close.

630
00:51:46,371 --> 00:51:48,239
Your life just got spared, sir.

631
00:51:54,612 --> 00:51:56,414
Man, I don't know how
it works in the city, but...

632
00:51:56,581 --> 00:51:57,715
trespassing around here

633
00:51:57,882 --> 00:51:59,550
usually ends with
a pine box and nails.

634
00:51:59,717 --> 00:52:01,085
We got shot at today.

635
00:52:03,188 --> 00:52:05,022
You get shot at
in these woods here?

636
00:52:05,556 --> 00:52:06,557
Yeah.

637
00:52:07,825 --> 00:52:09,660
- In these woods?
- In these woods.

638
00:52:09,827 --> 00:52:11,329
This afternoon.

639
00:52:13,231 --> 00:52:14,732
Well, that's odd,
Chris, 'cause...

640
00:52:15,166 --> 00:52:16,634
not many people
around here.

641
00:52:18,669 --> 00:52:20,338
Nobody hunts
around here but me.

642
00:52:21,939 --> 00:52:23,208
And were you hunting?

643
00:52:24,842 --> 00:52:25,976
This afternoon?

644
00:52:32,450 --> 00:52:33,584
Come on, Jake.

645
00:52:37,255 --> 00:52:39,224
I'm not sure how it
works in the country,

646
00:52:39,890 --> 00:52:41,091
but in the city,

647
00:52:41,626 --> 00:52:43,561
when someone shoots at you,
you don't wait for it

648
00:52:43,728 --> 00:52:44,829
to happen again.

649
00:52:50,701 --> 00:52:51,736
Hey.

650
00:52:54,171 --> 00:52:55,573
You be careful out there.

651
00:53:04,315 --> 00:53:05,416
You too.

652
00:53:40,985 --> 00:53:42,119
Can I help you?

653
00:53:43,187 --> 00:53:44,955
Yeah, yeah. Uh...

654
00:53:45,423 --> 00:53:46,557
my son here.

655
00:53:47,492 --> 00:53:48,693
His first season.

656
00:53:49,193 --> 00:53:50,528
Uh, looking for a rifle.

657
00:53:51,161 --> 00:53:52,563
Summer hunting or fall?

658
00:53:52,997 --> 00:53:53,998
What's-what's the difference?

659
00:53:54,164 --> 00:53:55,533
Oh, just the game. Uh...

660
00:53:56,166 --> 00:53:57,167
maybe the caliber.

661
00:53:57,368 --> 00:54:00,170
We got red squirrels,
sparrows, starlings,

662
00:54:00,338 --> 00:54:02,473
rock pigeons,
monk parakeets.

663
00:54:02,640 --> 00:54:04,675
Of course, come fall,
you got everything else.

664
00:54:04,875 --> 00:54:06,777
We're going to be hunting
bigger game, so, uh...

665
00:54:07,244 --> 00:54:08,346
I'd say fall.

666
00:54:08,946 --> 00:54:10,214
Deer or bear?

667
00:54:10,548 --> 00:54:12,817
Yeah. Uh... deer.

668
00:54:12,983 --> 00:54:14,585
Okay, well,
then you're probably looking

669
00:54:14,752 --> 00:54:16,454
for a mid-size caliber.

670
00:54:18,923 --> 00:54:22,059
That is a, uh, Browning
A-Bolt, extended barrel.

671
00:54:23,160 --> 00:54:24,895
You can hit a buck
a hundred yards away.

672
00:54:25,062 --> 00:54:26,030
Barely no slope.

673
00:54:27,131 --> 00:54:28,165
Yeah, I'll take it.

674
00:54:29,534 --> 00:54:31,369
Uh... good deal.

675
00:54:32,036 --> 00:54:35,373
Uh, I'm gonna need to see
some ID and a game license.

676
00:54:39,577 --> 00:54:40,778
Oh...

677
00:54:42,513 --> 00:54:44,815
You didn't grab Daddy's wallet
off the counter, did you?

678
00:54:46,517 --> 00:54:47,518
Oh, man.

679
00:54:47,752 --> 00:54:48,853
Um.

680
00:54:49,387 --> 00:54:50,455
You know what?

681
00:54:50,788 --> 00:54:52,222
My wife's card.

682
00:54:52,690 --> 00:54:54,592
I used it to grab some
groceries this morning.

683
00:54:54,759 --> 00:54:56,361
Maybe I could use this
for now?

684
00:54:56,527 --> 00:54:59,129
Bring back my paperwork
in the next day or so?

685
00:55:02,232 --> 00:55:03,634
You don't have no ID.

686
00:55:04,469 --> 00:55:06,504
You don't have a game license
or a money card

687
00:55:06,671 --> 00:55:08,038
with your name on it.

688
00:55:08,939 --> 00:55:11,376
And you want me to let you
walk outta here with a rifle?

689
00:55:35,299 --> 00:55:36,701
Let's get you in the car.

690
00:55:53,017 --> 00:55:54,284
If they're here,

691
00:55:54,785 --> 00:55:56,554
that mean we all
in danger, right?

692
00:55:58,556 --> 00:56:00,157
Maybe we tell Tara I'm here.

693
00:56:01,626 --> 00:56:02,993
Pissed as she might be,

694
00:56:03,394 --> 00:56:05,129
at least I'll be on
that side with you.

695
00:56:08,132 --> 00:56:09,333
I'm not scared.

696
00:56:09,934 --> 00:56:11,436
I'm just saying.

697
00:56:12,770 --> 00:56:14,271
Or maybe we call the cops.

698
00:56:15,305 --> 00:56:16,407
Cops?

699
00:56:18,275 --> 00:56:19,877
Don't think Hersh
knows 'em all by name?

700
00:56:22,346 --> 00:56:23,681
Don't be afraid, son.

701
00:56:24,248 --> 00:56:25,883
I won't let anything
happen to you.

702
00:56:26,917 --> 00:56:28,118
Load that up.

703
00:56:46,203 --> 00:56:47,572
Something happens to me...

704
00:56:48,338 --> 00:56:50,340
it's gonna be just you
to take care of your mom.

705
00:57:04,689 --> 00:57:05,723
You see it?

706
00:57:06,557 --> 00:57:07,925
Breathe.

707
00:57:10,427 --> 00:57:11,596
Pull the trigger.

708
00:57:14,565 --> 00:57:15,600
Pull it.

709
00:57:18,836 --> 00:57:20,037
Jake.

710
00:57:24,274 --> 00:57:25,342
You did it.

711
00:57:26,911 --> 00:57:28,979
Courage under stress.
Very good.

712
00:57:30,615 --> 00:57:31,749
Proud of you, son.

713
00:57:41,659 --> 00:57:43,561
Get behind me.
Get down, get down.

714
00:57:45,462 --> 00:57:46,997
You got three seconds
to come out!

715
00:57:48,332 --> 00:57:49,333
Three.

716
00:57:50,701 --> 00:57:51,702
Two.

717
00:57:53,170 --> 00:57:54,171
One!

718
00:58:15,960 --> 00:58:16,961
Jake!

719
00:58:34,612 --> 00:58:35,680
Jake.

720
00:58:36,781 --> 00:58:37,815
Don't move.

721
00:58:47,925 --> 00:58:49,126
Stay where you are, Jake.

722
00:59:02,907 --> 00:59:03,741
Ahh!

723
00:59:27,264 --> 00:59:29,199
What happened?
What happened, Chris?

724
00:59:29,600 --> 00:59:31,035
Chris, what happened?

725
00:59:31,235 --> 00:59:32,803
Come on. Okay, sit.

726
00:59:33,003 --> 00:59:33,971
Sit, sit, sit, sit.

727
00:59:34,138 --> 00:59:36,641
Okay, okay, okay.
Okay, baby.

728
00:59:36,874 --> 00:59:37,907
Jake, go to the bathroom.

729
00:59:37,908 --> 00:59:39,744
Go get my first aid kit,
uh, the toiletry kit.

730
00:59:39,910 --> 00:59:40,978
And some towels please.

731
00:59:41,278 --> 00:59:42,446
Baby, what happened?

732
00:59:42,613 --> 00:59:44,649
What happened, baby?
Tell me what happened.

733
00:59:52,256 --> 00:59:54,391
Lift up.

734
00:59:56,160 --> 00:59:57,527
Someone was out there.

735
00:59:58,528 --> 00:59:59,897
Before we got attacked.

736
01:00:01,531 --> 01:00:02,566
Watching us.

737
01:00:02,933 --> 01:00:04,401
Are you sure it wasn't...

738
01:00:05,202 --> 01:00:06,704
just someone in the woods?

739
01:00:06,971 --> 01:00:09,006
Hiking,
like you and Jake were.

740
01:00:09,173 --> 01:00:10,207
Yeah, I'm sure.

741
01:00:11,208 --> 01:00:13,243
I yelled for 'em
to come out, they hid.

742
01:00:14,411 --> 01:00:15,946
Maybe they were afraid.

743
01:00:16,113 --> 01:00:18,615
Why would they be afraid
of a guy and his kid walking?

744
01:00:18,983 --> 01:00:20,384
Well,
you said you were yelling.

745
01:00:21,051 --> 01:00:22,319
'Cause they were following us.

746
01:00:22,486 --> 01:00:23,754
Well, how do you know
they weren't just--

747
01:00:23,921 --> 01:00:26,056
Why are you so convinced
I didn't see what I saw?

748
01:00:35,299 --> 01:00:36,400
You're all done.

749
01:00:38,435 --> 01:00:39,737
I'm gonna go wash up.

750
01:01:17,674 --> 01:01:19,443
Help me get outta here,
please!

751
01:01:20,077 --> 01:01:22,046
Please! It's not right!

752
01:01:22,446 --> 01:01:24,248
Please help me get outta here!

753
01:01:24,882 --> 01:01:26,951
Please don't leave me.
Don't leave me!

754
01:01:30,921 --> 01:01:31,956
A developing system

755
01:01:32,122 --> 01:01:33,590
is moving in tonight
from the west,

756
01:01:33,758 --> 01:01:36,393
bringing increasing cloud
cover and rising pressure

757
01:01:36,560 --> 01:01:37,762
across the region.

758
01:01:37,928 --> 01:01:40,197
Skies will darken through
the early morning hours

759
01:01:40,364 --> 01:01:41,932
as that system
continues to build.

760
01:01:42,366 --> 01:01:44,601
Winds are expected
to pick up gradually.

761
01:01:44,769 --> 01:01:46,536
Steady at first,
then shifting direction

762
01:01:46,703 --> 01:01:48,172
as the front begins
to organize.

763
01:01:48,372 --> 01:01:51,075
By midday tomorrow,
scattered thunder is likely,

764
01:01:51,241 --> 01:01:54,278
with a chance
of more sustained activity
into the evening.

765
01:01:54,444 --> 01:01:56,480
- Hey.
- Hey. Morning.

766
01:02:00,484 --> 01:02:01,518
Can I help you?

767
01:02:02,686 --> 01:02:04,955
Oh, just doing my rounds,
checking on things.

768
01:02:06,190 --> 01:02:07,457
There's no one here but us.

769
01:02:11,728 --> 01:02:13,397
Yeah, I heard there was
some gunshots let off

770
01:02:13,563 --> 01:02:14,498
in the woods around here.

771
01:02:16,066 --> 01:02:17,301
You asking if it was me?

772
01:02:17,768 --> 01:02:19,937
No, I already know
the answer to that one.

773
01:02:22,139 --> 01:02:23,941
Wondering more what it means.

774
01:02:24,775 --> 01:02:26,844
I'm still not sure what
all of this has to do with me.

775
01:02:27,344 --> 01:02:28,779
Really?

776
01:02:31,248 --> 01:02:32,616
You're not the first
to travel this road.

777
01:02:32,783 --> 01:02:33,984
You don't have to do it alone.

778
01:02:37,221 --> 01:02:38,455
You're trying
to get in my head.

779
01:02:38,622 --> 01:02:40,524
I'm trying to offer you
some grace here, man.

780
01:02:40,690 --> 01:02:41,591
Who are you to give me grace?

781
01:02:41,758 --> 01:02:42,860
- A friend?
- A friend.

782
01:02:43,227 --> 01:02:44,228
When did that happen?

783
01:02:44,394 --> 01:02:45,662
Maybe when some weapons
went missing

784
01:02:45,830 --> 01:02:47,064
in the gun shop parking lot.

785
01:02:47,731 --> 01:02:50,267
Or the dead wolf.
Or the-the trail of blood.

786
01:02:51,235 --> 01:02:53,137
I'd appreciate it if you
didn't come by anymore.

787
01:02:55,139 --> 01:02:56,540
Not while we're still here.

788
01:03:01,111 --> 01:03:02,712
You think he's
connected to the case?

789
01:03:03,713 --> 01:03:05,082
I don't know.

790
01:03:06,050 --> 01:03:07,952
Trying to put it all together.

791
01:03:09,920 --> 01:03:11,021
What about Tara?

792
01:03:12,990 --> 01:03:14,724
It was her idea
to bring you out here.

793
01:03:16,260 --> 01:03:18,028
She got the ball rolling
on the settlement.

794
01:03:19,997 --> 01:03:21,331
Between her and Hersh...

795
01:03:23,200 --> 01:03:24,501
I'm just saying.

796
01:03:26,703 --> 01:03:28,305
Gotta keep our eyes open.

797
01:03:31,408 --> 01:03:32,742
Keep Jake close.

798
01:05:41,005 --> 01:05:42,039
Chris?

799
01:07:02,352 --> 01:07:03,387
You're up.

800
01:07:04,654 --> 01:07:05,889
I'm up.

801
01:07:09,759 --> 01:07:12,796
So, when's the, um,
big reveal?

802
01:07:13,163 --> 01:07:14,664
For
that thing you're building.

803
01:07:16,900 --> 01:07:18,302
There's nothing to reveal.

804
01:07:18,935 --> 01:07:19,936
I'm just building.

805
01:07:20,670 --> 01:07:21,605
Really.

806
01:07:22,972 --> 01:07:24,040
Well, um...

